# Fastlane / CI parity (mandatory for agents)

Validate iOS changes with the **same commands GitHub Actions runs**. Do not substitute raw `xcodebuild` or isolated `scripts/ci/*` calls for “did CI pass?” checks.

## Required commands (repo root)

```bash
bundle install   # once per machine / after Gemfile change
```

| Goal | Command | CI workflow |
|------|---------|---------------|
| Tests + coverage gate | `bundle exec fastlane test` | `.github/workflows/ci.yml` |
| TestFlight archive/upload | `bundle exec fastlane beta` | `.github/workflows/deploy-testflight.yml` |

Run from the **repository root** (`knowledge-base-app-ios/`), not from `fastlane/`.

## Before push to `main`

1. **`bundle exec fastlane test`** — must pass; lane enforces **≥ 35%** line coverage on `KnowledgeBaseApp.app`.
2. If you changed **`fastlane/Fastfile`**, deploy workflows, or release scripts: re-read the lane — internal steps use paths relative to the Fastfile (`__dir__`), not the shell cwd.

Full **`beta`** needs Match + ASC secrets (CI / local env). Agents cannot skip `test` and assume `beta` will work.

## Do NOT use for CI parity

- `xcodebuild test` / `xcodebuild build` instead of `fastlane test` before push
- `bash scripts/ci/sync_marketing_version.sh` (or other deploy scripts) **standalone** to “verify the build” — these run **inside** `fastlane beta` and Deploy workflow
- Direct `scan` / `gym` / `xcodebuild` with custom flags that differ from the Fastfile

## Allowed outside Fastlane

- `xcodegen generate` after editing `project.yml` (then commit `.xcodeproj`)
- `bash scripts/ci/check_no_hardcoded_cyrillic.sh` (also in CI; lightweight lint)
- Editing `VERSION` / `CHANGELOG.md` without running deploy scripts locally

## Why

Fastlane sets up CI (`setup_ci`), picks simulator (`SCAN_DEVICE`), coverage gate, signing for Release, and resolves script paths. Calling scripts or `xcodebuild` directly caused drift (e.g. `sync_marketing_version.sh` not found when cwd was `fastlane/`).

